Rules:
- Use ONLY the evidence above. Every claim lists the ids of the evidence that supports it in
  evidence_ids, using the ids exactly as shown (for example C1-E03). Claims without a valid
  evidence id are discarded automatically.
- executive_summary: 2-4 claims - what {{ competitor }} is doing and what it means for us.
- marketing_activity: campaigns, launches, pricing moves, partnerships and channel activity.
- analyst_commentary: what analysts, rating agencies and researchers say - cite analyst items
  only; return an empty list when there are none.
- community_signals: what customers and online communities say - cite community items only;
  return an empty list when there are none.
- next_best_actions: 3-6 actions for {{ brand.name }}, each with a priority - P1 act this week
  (high impact, time-sensitive), P2 this month, P3 monitor - an owner_role (e.g. Head of Brand,
  Pricing lead, Sales enablement), a one-sentence rationale and the evidence ids behind it.
- event_notes: for each high-impact event id above, one sentence on why it matters to {{ brand.name }}.
- Keep each claim to one sentence. Do not repeat the same evidence across sections unless it is
  genuinely relevant to both.
